344-                  Effect of treatments on soil pH and growth of lettuce
345:                  As presented in Table 2, all stabilization treatments but CHB significantly increased soil
346-                  pH over the spiked control in PK soil. In BA soil, addition of FMB had non-significant
347-                  effect on soil pH, whereas all other treatments significantly increased the pH of the soil
348-                  compared to the spiked control. Similar to this study, the findings of several studies indi-
349-                  cated that the application of biochar and alkaline amendments enhanced soil pH (Chan
350-                  et al. 2007, 2008; Lee et al. 2008; Ok et al. 2011a, b). Among the stabilization treatments,
351-                  LI and ES promoted the greatest pH increase in both soils, mainly due to the alkaline
352-                  impact of LI and ES (lime-based material) containing CaCO3, which dissociate to Ca2+
353-                  and CO32−, consequently the reaction of CO32− with water liberate OH−1 ions, thereby
354-                  resulting in soil pH increase (Ok et al. 2011a; Lee et al. 2013).
